      <memberdef kind="function" id="history_8h_1a867aecd470d427b62ac12eb938b584cf" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>char *</type>
        <definition>char * history_file_path</definition>
        <argsstring>(void)</argsstring>
        <name>history_file_path</name>
        <param>
          <type>void</type>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Determine the path to the history file based on environment variables. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Follows POSIX-compliant lookup order: first checks $HISTFILE, then falls back to $HOME/.sh_history. Returns a malloc&apos;d string that the caller must free. <simplesect kind="return"><para>A malloc&apos;d string with the history file path, or NULL if neither variable is set or valid. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
