        <definition>void history_load</definition>
        <argsstring>(const char *file_path)</argsstring>
        <name>history_load</name>
        <param>
          <type>const char *</type>
          <declname>file_path</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Load the command history from a file into readline&apos;s in-memory history list. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This function uses readline&apos;s <computeroutput>read_history()</computeroutput> to populate the history list. If <computeroutput>file_path</computeroutput> is NULL, this function does nothing. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>file_path</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The path to the history file to load, or NULL to skip loading. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
